  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A parentheses string is valid exactly when:\n\n* It is the empty string,\n* It can be written as `AB` (`A` concatenated with `B`), where `A` and `B` are valid strings, or\n* It can be written as `(A)`, where `A` is a valid string.\n\nYou receive a parentheses string `s`. In one move, you can insert a parenthesis at any position of the string.\n\n* As an example, if `s = \"()))\"`, you can insert an opening parenthesis to be `\"(()))\"` or a closing parenthesis to be `\"())))\"`.\n\nOutput *the smallest number of moves required to make* `s` *valid*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"())\"\nOutput: 1\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"(((\"\nOutput: 3\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 1000`\n* `s[i]` is either `'('` or `')'`.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
    "sampleTestCases": [
